#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

cat <<'EOF'
coherence-core-db

Coherence-compatible Rust CLI tool workflow

Start:
  make tool doctor       check dependencies and repo state
  make tool context      understand why this project exists
  make tool next         fetch next task + minimal viable context
  make tool bootstrap-tasks prepare/import BOOT-* task seeds for beads

Planning:
  make tool plan         HITL planning loop [stub]

Implementation:
  make tool run          fmt/check/test/policy checks (workspace tests run under isolated profile)
  make test-isolated      cargo test workspace (explicit isolated profile helper)
  make smoke / smoke-isolated   m0 + m1 Dolt smoke (isolated-by-default wrappers)
  make test-world-reset  remove repo-local .dolt (requires COHERENCE_DB_PROFILE=test; Makefile sets this)

Review:
  make tool present-work create review package [partial]
  make tool feedback     read feedback and choose next loop [partial]

Dolt:
  make tool dolt-start
  make tool dolt-status
  make tool dolt-stop
  make tool migrate

ADR-0006 (optional user-scoped shared server):
  export COHERENCE_USE_USER_SCOPED_DOLT=1
  then make tool dolt-start / dolt-stop / dolt-status (same commands).
  Layout:
    • data-dir:      ${COHERENCE_DOLT_DATA_DIR:-${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/coherence/db}
    • runtime-dir:   ${COHERENCE_DOLT_RUNTIME_DIR:-$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/coherence}
                       (when XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is unset: ${HOME}/.cache/coherence/run)
    • socket:        ${DOLT_SOCKET:-<runtime-dir>/dolt.sock}
  Select project DB with DOLT_DB=<slug>. Embedded migrations still connect via loopback TCP; internal port defaults to 33306 (override COHERENCE_DOLT_TCP_PORT).
  Repo-local .dolt sql-server remains the default when COHERENCE_USE_USER_SCOPED_DOLT is unset (CI/agents).
  Scripted verification: ./scripts/user-scoped-dolt-smoke.sh
  Isolated tests (make test-isolated, make tool run) under user-scoped: ./scripts/with-isolated-test-profile exports a fresh DOLT_DB=coherence_test_<uuid> (override prefix with COHERENCE_TEST_DB_PREFIX), then coherence-core-db drop-isolated-test-db after a successful run. Set COHERENCE_KEEP_TEST_WORLD (non-empty) to skip dropping after failure or success; on child failure with keep, stderr prints a COHERENCE_PRESERVED_TEST_WORLD block (DOLT_SOCKET, DOLT_DB, optional COHERENCE_ISOLATED_TEST_RUN_ID). Quiet success does not print that block; set COHERENCE_ISOLATED_TEST_VERBOSE=1 for allocation logging and for the block after success+keep. Teardown only drops names matching that prefix.

Canonical repository database policy (ADR-0004):
  this checkout's Dolt catalog is curated reasoning state — do not mutate it from tests
  workspace tests require COHERENCE_DB_PROFILE=test and a disposable Dolt target (make test-isolated, make tool run)
  mutating smoke (writes fixtures) uses the same profile — use make smoke from repo root, not raw m*-smoke without env
  optional teardown of a disposable catalog: make tool dolt-stop then make test-world-reset (omit reset after a failure if you need forensics)
  full operator lifecycle: AGENTS.md

Coherence DB ownership:
  one repository = one logical Coherence DB catalog (repo-local .dolt server by default)
  preferred local socket when repo-local: .dolt/dolt.sock
  optional shared server socket when ADR-0006: see COHERENCE_USE_USER_SCOPED_DOLT above
  cross-repo coordination uses links/contracts/commits/versions, not shared writes
  consumer repos must not write into dependency/vendor repos' Dolt DBs
  core-db owns shared conventions and future workspace indexing, not this repo's truth

Docs/policy:
  make tool docs-export  NOT_IMPLEMENTED
  make tool check-policy enforce root Markdown/docs policy

Backend:
  workflow_backend: local_stub
  orchestration_owner: external
  external_future_backend: temporal_candidate
  event_signal_hooks: NOT_IMPLEMENTED

Orchestration:
  Generated CLI tools expose stable local commands only.
  External coherence-orchestrator/coherence-worker may use Temporal later.
  Do not configure Temporal URLs, namespaces, task queues, or workflow IDs here.

Contracts:
  coherence-contracts: external dependency
  proto definitions: NOT_IMPLEMENTED here; do not duplicate contracts in this repo
  runtime blocker: false
  local proto definitions: false
  future path: consume versioned contracts from coherence-contracts when tooling exists

Dependency policy:
  beads-deliverables/bdx: required
  workgate: optional policy enforcer

Task tracking:
  BOOT seed file: tasks/beads-tasks.ndjson
  Start tracking: make tool bootstrap-tasks
  Missing beads: command reports prepared/degraded state without blocking local workflow

Rules:
  docs/ is generated/read-only
  root Markdown is forbidden except AGENTS.md
EOF
